        "zoom": [
          1,
          1.05
        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Pero el libro antiguo cuenta algo más. De noche, a veces, la tierra lloraba.",
          "en": "But the old book tells one more thing. Sometimes, at night, the earth would cry."
        },
        {
          "es": "Decían que tenía hambre, y que no daría frutos si no recibía ofrendas.",
          "en": "People said she was hungry, and that she would not give fruit unless she received offerings."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los mexicas creían que la tierra y el sol necesitaban ofrendas, incluso vidas humanas. Por eso hacían sacrificios.",
          "en": "The Mexica believed the earth and the sun needed offerings, even human lives. That is why they made sacrifices."
        },
        {
          "es": "Para ellos era como una deuda: la tierra nos alimenta, y había que devolverle algo.",
          "en": "To them it was like a debt: the earth feeds us, so something had to be given back."
        }
      ],
